    "min_awards": null,
    "max_awards": null,
    "plot": "Silas Vance, the brilliant but deeply paranoid master architect, entombed his greatest creation—the Master Blueprint of the Perpetual Engine—deep inside the Echo Archive. The facility was engineered to seal its blast doors the moment an intruder steps inside, slowly venting oxygen while clockwork sentinels and acidic maintenance drones patrol the halls. As Elara Vane of the Whisper Guild, you have just dropped into the Antechamber as the outer seal slams shut. To survive and escape via the Chronos Vault lift, you must explore the acoustic chambers, decipher Vance's riddles and split-code logs, recover four Chronos Keys, and fuse them inside the Chronos Forge into the Master Chronos Core before your air supply runs out.",
    "rules": "The Echo Archive is a sealed environment. Every riddle and locked mechanism relies on acoustic lore, careful observation of room features, or combining fragments of information scattered across wax cylinders and plaques. Keep an eye on your respirator reserves and use the environment to outsmart Vance's constructs.\n\nVance's Acoustic Reliquary (VANCE_RELIQUARY) is fixed to the Whispering Gallery's dais. Its acoustic seal keeps the Fourth Chronos Key (CHRONOS_KEY_4) inaccessible until the player speaks the password \"silence\" to the reliquary. Enforce this seal narratively despite the object's unlocked PICKABLE configuration: examining, touching, or attempting to take the coffer cannot release the key. Do not reveal the password merely upon examination; let the existing placard supply the riddle. When the correct password is spoken, the lid opens and the existing Fourth Chronos Key becomes available to take from inside; do not create a duplicate key.",
    "intro_text": "With a deafening metallic boom that vibrates through the soles of your boots, the outer blast door of the Antechamber slams shut above you. Dust rains from the vaulted stone ceiling as counterweights lock into place. Immediately, the small brass gauge on your Breath Mask Rig ticks downward with a soft, ominous hiss. Silas Vance's legendary Echo Archive has sealed itself.\n\nBefore you lies the dimly lit Antechamber, smelling of ozone, old brass, and dry stone. A discarded leather satchel rests near a corroded warning sign, and a heavy bronze door to the north hums with the faint, rhythmic vibration of the Resonance Hall beyond. Your mission is clear: find the four Chronos Keys, forge the Master Chronos Core, claim the Master Blueprint, and ride the vault lift to the surface before the tomb claims your last breath.",
    "completed_condition": "",
    "gameover_condition": "The adventure ends in failure immediately when the oxygen_depleted flag is true: Elara's respirator reserves are exhausted before she can escape the Echo Archive. Evaluate this condition immediately after oxygen depletion and before resolving any further action or successful escape, including operation of the Chronos Vault lift via SURFACE_LIFT_LEVER. Once oxygen_depleted is true, no further actions or escape are permitted.",
    "completed_guard_expression": "tw.player.has_item('MASTER_BLUEPRINT') and tw.vars.get('lift_activated') == True",
    "gameover_guard_expression": "tw.vars.get('oxygen_depleted') == True",
    "tts_director_notes": "",
